423:
The chief of police, or city police officers under his or her direction, shall:
A. Attend any meetings of the council at the request of the council or city manager;
B. Execute all orders and directions of the city manager;
C. Abate or remove any nuisance when so directed by the city manager upon order of the council;
D. Maintain the peace, good order and tranquility of the city by the enforcement of all municipal ordinances and state or federal laws;
E. Under the general direction of the city manager, be in charge of the police department and have supervision over the members thereof in the exercise of their powers, duties and authority and in hiring, discharging or suspending any members within the parameters of City of Marietta charter, ordinances, rules and regulations, civil service laws, and any other appropriate statute;
F. Should any arrested person be jailed at the order of a city police officer, enter or cause to be entered the name of the person arrested, the date of arrest, and the name of the arresting officer or other person, in the computer records;
G. Serve all subpoenas and warrants of the municipal court and city council and as otherwise authorized by law;
H. Approve appearance bonds as provided in Section 1-12-060 of this Code;
I. Issue and serve summons for any violation of any law or ordinance and serve all processes, executions, attachments and the like for the city clerk, municipal court or the city council; notwithstanding however that civilian parking enforcement officers may issue parking citations and conduct the booting process;
J. Render such aid and assistance to the Cobb County Health Director as may be necessary to enforce in the city all health laws of this state and regulations pertaining to health of the city.
(Code 1978 § 2-1001; Ord. No. 5575, 6/12/96; Ord. No. 7004, 1/10/2007, § 1)

446:
There is established the position of city emergency management director. The fire chief or a designee thereof shall act as the city emergency management director. The director shall be charged with the following duties:
A. To represent the city manager on matters pertaining to natural or manmade emergencies or disasters at interagency or interjurisdiction meetings;
B. To assist city officials in organizing city departments for emergency/disaster operations;
C. To develop, in conjunction with city departments and agencies, an operational plan for use by the city crisis management team. This plan shall be in consonance with the state and federal emergency operation plans. The plan shall be submitted to the city council and thence to the state or federal agencies for approval as may be necessary;
D. To carry out the day to day administration of emergency/crisis preparedness and disaster program which may include the rendering of required reports to the state emergency management agency through the appropriate local emergency management agency; and
E. To render reports such as may be necessary which document such items as event financial statements, activity reports, incident action plans and event critique as required by the city manager in keeping with good business practices.
F. The city emergency management director shall be attached to the office of the city manager and shall be under the general direction of the city manager.
G. The city emergency management director shall coordinate with the appropriate state, federal or mutual aid group in the planning, training and implementation of disaster operations.
(Code 1978, § 2-3002; Ord. No. 5575, 6/12/96)

